humbnail":""},{"id":"1775589786467","neuronKeys":["[#d9507]"],"edgeStrings":["[#b5f52]_#_[#d9507]","[#d9507]_#_[#3535d]"],"description":"When a sound is heared that is very quiet to extremely loud, it will cause the first neuron to emit a faint glow.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775589824145","neuronKeys":["[#8f8d7]"],"edgeStrings":["[#8f8d7]_#_[#3535d]","[#b5f52]_#_[#8f8d7]"],"description":"When Spikerbot hears a sound that is a bit louder to extremely loud, it will emit a slightly brighter glow that will add to the softer glow of the first neuron.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775589876429","neuronKeys":["[#680c2]"],"edgeStrings":["[#b5f52]_#_[#680c2]","[#680c2]_#_[#3535d]"],"description":"The third neuron will respond to someone talking at a normal level through hearing something very loud, and when it lights up spikerbot, the previous two neurons will add to the light together.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775589941015","neuronKeys":["[#d51d5]"],"edgeStrings":["[#b5f52]_#_[#d51d5]","[#d51d5]_#_[#3535d]"],"description":"The final neuron listens only to louder noises. It will make the lights glow as bright as they go!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775590013664","neuronKeys":[],"edgeStrings":["[#b5f52]_#_[#d9507]","[#b5f52]_#_[#8f8d7]","[#b5f52]_#_[#680c2]","[#b5f52]_#_[#d51d5]"],"description":"Experiment with the volume ranges spikerbot listens to, if the loud neuron triggers to early, you can change the input to make SpikerBot’s hearing less sensitive.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775590054751","neuronKeys":[],"edgeStrings":["[#d51d5]_#_[#3535d]"],"description":"Try changing the colors and which lights will trigger. Perhaps you can set an alarm when the volume is too high, and even make spikerbot make a noise as well!","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"Volume Meter","description":"Spikerbot will glow brighter and brighter the louder you get!","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-08T16:05:16.935063"}}